{title: 159 - The Old Rugged Cross}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #159 • THE OLD RUGGED CROSS • 11.9.12.9}
{lyricist: George Bennard}
{composer: George Bennare}
{key: Ab}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 159}
{meta: tune THE OLD RUGGED CROSS}
{meta: meter 11.9.12.9}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Ab]On a hill far [Db/Ab]away [Ab]stood an [Db]old rugged [Eb7/Db]cross,
[Bbm]The emblem [Eb7]of [Ab/Eb]suffering [Eb7]and [Ab]shame,
[Ab]And I love [Db/Ab]that [Ab]old cross [Db]where the dearest [Eb7]and best
[Eb7]For [Ab/Eb]a [Eb7]world [Ab]of [Eb]lost sinners [Eb7]was slain.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Eb7]So I'll cherish [Ab/C]the old [Db]rugged cross,
[Db]till my trophies [Ab]at last I lay down;
[Ab]I will [Db/Ab]cling to [Ab]the old [Db]rugged cross,
[Db]and exchange [Eb7]it [Ab/Eb]some [Eb7]day for a [Ab]crown.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Ab]O that old rugged [Db/Ab]cross, [Ab]so despised [Db]by the [Eb7/Db]world,
[Bbm]has a [Eb7]wondrous [Ab/Eb]attraction [Eb7]for [Ab]me;
[Ab]for the dear [Db/Ab]Lamb [Ab]of God [Db]left his glory [Eb7]above
[Eb7]to [Ab/Eb]bear [Eb7]it [Ab]to [Eb]dark Calvary.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Ab]To that old rugged [Db/Ab]cross [Ab]I will ever [Db]be [Eb7/Db]true,
[Bbm]its [Eb7]shame and [Ab/Eb]reproach [Eb7]gladly [Ab]bear;
[Ab]then he'll call [Db/Ab]me [Ab]some day [Db]to my home [Bbm]far [Eb7]away,
[Eb7]where [Ab/Eb]his [Eb7]glory [Eb]forever [Eb7]I'll share.
{end_of_verse}
